# Citation metadata for this repository (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
#
# To complete before the Zenodo release (submission checklist A4, A7):
#   - the author list, to match the manuscript's; only contributors who can
#     be identified from the repository are listed so far
#   - version, date-released and doi, once the release is minted
#   - preferred-citation, once the article is published
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this analysis or its results, please cite it using these
  metadata. A citation for the associated article will be added when it is
  published.
type: software
title: >-
  Sockeye salmon TagSeq: gonad and liver gene expression in territorial and
  social Oncorhynchus nerka
abstract: >-
  Complete analysis for a comparison of gonad and liver transcriptomes of adult
  sockeye salmon classified at capture as territorial or social, measured by
  3' tag RNA sequencing: DESeq2 differential expression, GO and KEGG
  over-representation, the manuscript's figures and supplementary tables, and
  a check that re-running the analysis reproduces every committed result.
authors:
  - given-names: Steven
    family-names: Roberts
    affiliation: School of Aquatic and Fishery Sciences, University of Washington
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8302-1138"
  - alias: mattgeorgephd
repository-code: "https://github.com/RobertsLab/project-sockeye-tagseq"
url: "https://robertslab.github.io/project-sockeye-tagseq/"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - sockeye salmon
  - Oncorhynchus nerka
  - TagSeq
  - territoriality
  - gene expression
  - DESeq2
  - reproducibility
